# Generated by scripts/celegans_fates.py (genomeos.organism.fate_rules): terminal fates from the
# measured factors (Ma et al. 2021), read as integrated along the lineage path. Imported after the lineage program, so a
# factor rule overrides the observed fate of a terminal cell and the lookup stays the fallback.
# The Body fires every applying differentiate decision in order and the last wins: precedence runs
# bottom to top.
module organism.celegans.fates
import cell_types.bio

decision factor_fate_23 { action: differentiate; when: cell_type = Coelomocyte|Epithelium|Excretory|Gland|GliaSheath|GliaSocket|Hypodermis|Intestine|Mesoderm|Muscle|Neuron|Other|PharyngealMarginal|Rectal|Reproductive|TailSpike|Valve, stage = Cleavage|Gastrulation|Morphogenesis, CEH-27_integrated = present, EFL-3_integrated = present; to: Neuron; evidence: inferred "learned from Ma 2021 x WormWeb (precision 1.0, n 3); factors Ma et al. 2021, Nat Methods 18:893 (Zenodo 4737593)"; confidence: 0.7 }
